    "rich_text_intro": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A one-pan dinner that happens to have four kinds of seafood in it. Onion, garlic and cherry tomatoes cook down until the tomatoes burst and go jammy, cannellini beans go in with a little of their liquid, and then the part that makes the dish: four ripe tomatoes juiced straight into the pan, skins left behind. That is the broth. No stock cube, no tin.</p><p>Shrimp poach in it, kale wilts into it, and the salmon and branzino are crisped separately and broken over the top so the skin stays crisp. Salmon roe at the end, and bread for the bottom of the pan.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
