            "icon": "time",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "About 45 minutes",
            "text": "<p>Most of it is the base reducing while you prep. The seafood is the last ten minutes and goes fast &mdash; have everything peeled and dry before you start it.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_serves": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "users",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Serves 4",
            "text": "<p>Straight from the skillet. Scales to six with another fillet and a second cup of beans; the pan just needs to be wide enough not to steam.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_omega": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "heart",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Four proteins, one pan",
            "text": "<p>King salmon, branzino, black tiger shrimp and salmon roe. Each brings a different texture, which is the reason to use all four rather than doubling one.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
