    "game_plan": {
      "type": "timeline",
      "blocks": {
        "s_thaw": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_3532_e1e22abb-19cf-4c34-a607-dd2e93594488.heic",
            "subheading": "The night before",
            "heading": "Thaw everything in the refrigerator",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Move the sealed packs from the freezer to the refrigerator about 12 hours ahead &mdash; salmon, branzino, shrimp and the roe tin. In a hurry, submerge the sealed packs in cold water for 20&ndash;30 minutes. Never at room temperature.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_prep": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_5323_0a65944b-cda8-40a4-be0c-1c3cd8430de3.heic",
            "subheading": "Step 1",
            "heading": "Dry the fish, salt it, peel the shrimp",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Pat both fillets dry with an unbleached paper towel &mdash; drier than feels necessary, skin especially &mdash; then salt the flesh and the skin generously. Peel the shrimp. Set it all aside while you build the base.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_base": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_5324_eab7718e-a2ee-4aa1-aad1-61e8a7e431b5.heic",
            "subheading": "Step 2",
            "heading": "Onion, garlic, chili, then tomatoes until jammy",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Olive oil in a large skillet over medium. Onion, garlic, a pinch of salt and the chili flakes until soft and fragrant. Add the cherry tomatoes and leave them until they burst and go jammy, then stir in the cannellini beans with a little of their liquid.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_broth": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_5334_00f31ac1-d0f1-4149-a693-57ef0d672b41.heic",
            "subheading": "Step 3",
            "heading": "Juice the tomatoes in, add kale, reduce",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Squeeze the four ripe tomatoes straight into the pan and discard the skins. Sun-dried tomatoes and rosemary in, then let it simmer and reduce, loosening with vegetable broth until it is rich and spoonable. Kale in until just wilted, then lemon zest.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
